==Icelandic==

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|is|/ˈhaːva/}}
*: {{rhymes|is|aːva|s=2}}

===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|is|non|hafa}}, from {{der|is|gem-pro|*habjaną}}, from {{der|is|ine-pro|*keh₂p-||take, seize}}.

====Verb====
{{is-verb-weak|hafði|haft}}

# {{lb|is|transitive|governs the accusative}} to [[have]]
#: {{ux|is|''Ég '''hef''' ekki tíma í kvöldmat.''|I don't '''have''' time for dinner.}}
#: {{ux|is|''María [[hafa áhuga á|'''hefur''' áhuga á]] stjórnmálum.''|Maria is interested in politics.}}
# {{lb|is|transitive|governs the accusative}} to [[hold]], to [[have]]
# {{lb|is|transitive|governs the accusative}} to [[keep]]
# {{lb|is|transitive|governs the accusative}} to [[feel]]
#: {{ux|is|''Hvernig '''hefurðu''' það?'' - ''Ég '''hef''' það fínt.''|How are you '''doing'''? - I'm fine.}}

=====Usage notes=====
* '''hafa''' is most often an [[auxiliary verb]] ([[hjálparsögn]]) which is followed by the [[past participle]]. The [[participle]] is in the [[neuter]] [[singular]] with '''hafa''':
*: {{ux|is|''Ég '''hef''' oft '''gert''' það.''|I''''ve done''' it many times.}}
* When '''hafa''' is the [[main verb]] it's used to indicate something [[abstract]], e.g. [[time]], [[experience]], [[interest]] etc.:
*: {{ux|is|''Ég '''hef''' [[nógur|nógan]] [[tími|tíma]].''|I have enough time.}}
* Note that the verb '''hafa''' is not used as the English "[[have]]" in the sense of possession of an object. The verb {{m|is|eiga}} is used in the same way as the verb "[[have]]":
*: {{ux|is|''Við [[eiga|eigum]] [[hundur|hund]].''|We [[have]] a [[dog]].}}

=====Conjugation=====
{{is-conj (hafa)}}
Note: The forms ''hefi'' — ''hefir'' — ''hefir'' are fairly rare, but acceptable.

